{
  "family": "Civilcon I beams (South Africa, beam & slab construction)",
  "description": "South African standard pretensioned I beams I1-I20 (710-1980 mm deep) per the Civilcon PPBI datasheet (TMH7 NA+NB loading span charts). These are the British-tradition SA I-beams. Profile decoded exactly from the PPBI vector drawing: B1 = top flange width, B2 = top flange width at its base (slight side taper), B3 = web width, B4 = bottom flange width (vertical sides), D2/D3/D4/D5/D6 = top flange / upper splay / web / lower splay (45 deg) / bottom flange depths, summing exactly to D1. The drawing shows the as-cast orientation (B1 face down); published 'Yb over soffit' is measured from the B1 face.",
  "sources": {
    "properties_and_dims": "Civilcon (Pretoria) PPBI.pdf precast I-beam datasheet - dimensions, section properties (gamma = 25 kN/m3) and TMH7 NA+NB span charts.",
